   "evidence": "`real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq` is a plain `theorem`, not simp (upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Basic.lean:398), so nothing normalizes `inner \u211d kT kT`. The sibling module states the convention explicitly: \"The exceptions are the squares ... these are `@[simp]`\" (GPD/Kinematics.lean:31-33), and indeed `minkowskiProduct_avgMomentum_self_eq` and `minkowskiProduct_deltaOrthN_self_eq` carry it.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/LightFront.lean",
   "fix": "Tag `minkowskiProduct_ofLightFront_self` `@[simp]` (give it a higher priority than `minkowskiProduct_ofLightFront` if the general rule still wins on the square).",
   "issue": "`minkowskiProduct_ofLightFront_self` (the square, normal form `2ab - \u2016kT\u2016\u00b2`) is not `@[simp]`, while the general pairing `minkowskiProduct_ofLightFront` at line 410 is. On a square, simp applies the general rule and stops at `a*b + b*a - inner \u211d kT kT`, never reaching the file's `\u2016\u00b7\u2016^2` normal form (`minkowskiProduct_self_eq_lightFront`, line 311).",
